icate from the default response:"},"1627":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#enroll-the-device","content":"If curl fails, use Troubleshooting with the saved body. Do not convert it or repeat the request without querying inventory: a timeout or error can follow persisted issuance."},"1628":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#verify-the-obtained-identity","content":"Expect `device.crt: OK` and exit code 0 from `cmp`. Check the CN, serial, dates, Digital Signature and Client Authentication. The certificate must be a leaf: it must not declare `CA:TRUE` or Certificate Sign use. Check that its validity matches the one-hour profile."},"1629":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#verify-the-obtained-identity","content":"In Lamassu, open `est-device-001`. It must be created with the intended owning DMS, a current identity and the received certificate in its history. Compare the local serial with the slot; thresholds can show a renewal state rather than simply Active."},"1630":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"In a second terminal, enter the same directory and run `umask 077`. Create a local server certificate and start a test consumer. This server trusts `device-root.pem` and requires a valid client identity:"},"1631":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Leave it running. In the first terminal, connect using the obtained identity:"},"1632":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Expect HTTP `200`. The client's trust in this local server is its self-signed `consumer.crt`; the server verifies the device against `device-root.pem`. The HTML file displays OpenSSL diagnostic information."},"1633":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"With the same server still running, test that a request without a client certificate is rejected:"},"1634":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/iot-fleets/quickstarts/enroll-device#demonstrate-an-mtls-connection","content":"Rejection must correspond to a missing certificate at the server, not a stopped server. Stop the consumer with Ctrl+C after the test. This exercise demonstrates TLS authentication and key possession; y