66":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`8090`"},"2967":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"hawkBit server, only for hawkBit mode"},"2968":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`rustfs`"},"2969":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`9000` (S3), `9001` (console)"},"2970":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"Local S3 store, only with `--profile s3`"},"2971":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#services","content":"`docker compose --profile s3 up -d` also starts `rustfs` and `s3-init`, which creates the encrypted bucket `ota-updates` that artifacts, builds and hawkBit's artifact storage can use. Without that profile, and with `config-docker.yml`, artifacts and builds stay on the `update_files` volume."},"2972":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#verify-the-api","content":"The second call reports the active backend and what it supports. In native mode it looks like this (shortened):"},"2973":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#verify-the-api","content":"`supported` has one entry for each of the 22 capabilities. See Capabilities for what each one means."},"2974":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"Start the monolithic entry point with a config file. It runs the Updates API and SymKMS together."},"2975":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"If `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` is not set, the service reads `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml`."},"2976":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"To build `.swu` files outside Docker, install `swugenerator` into the Python environment that the config points at (the image does the same from `swugenerator/requirements.txt`):"},"2977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"The `config.yml` at the repository root is a starting point for local development, not a ready-made file:"},"2978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It needs Postgres (`localhost:5000`) and the WFX management API (`localhost:9081`), which `docker compose up -d postgres custom-wfx` provides."},"2979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It contains values for one developer machine: absolute `/home/alvaro/...` paths for artifact and SymKMS storage, the signer script and `swugenerator`, and a LAN IP for the Lamassu endpoints. Edit them to paths the service user can create; the service stops at start-up if it cannot create its directories."},"2980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#run-without-docker","content":"It stores artifacts and build outputs in the local RustFS bucket (`docker compose --profile s3 up -d`). To use local disk instead, remove the `artifacts:` and `builds:` blocks; when they are absent, artifacts default to `{update_files_base_dir}/artifacts`."},"2981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#try-hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit mode serves the same API on top of a real hawkBit server. Start hawkBit and Postgres, wait until hawkBit answers, then start the service with the hawkBit config:"},"2982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#try-hawkbit-mode","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml` also contains developer-machine paths, in the SWU build settings. A service pointed at a hawkBit with no registered devices builds and launches normally, but nothing downloads the update, because in hawkBit mode devices poll hawkBit directly. Read hawkBit mode before using it."},"2983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"2984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"Likely cause"},"2985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`docker compose up` fails on the network"},"2986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`ota-net` does not exist. Run `docker network create ota-net`"},"2987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The `updates` container cannot reach Lamassu"},"2988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`HOST_IP` is empty in `.env`, or `dms_endpoint` in `config-docker.yml` points at an address the container cannot reach"},"2989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"`docker compose up --build` fails while copying `lamassuiot/core`"},"2990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The build context (the parent of `ota/`) does not contain `lamassuiot/`"},"2991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"The service exits at start-up when run on the host"},"2992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started#troubleshooting","content":"A directory in the config (`update_files_base_dir`, `sym_keys_dir`) cannot be created, or Postgres or WFX is not reachable at the addresses in the file"},"2993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-started-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/getting-