t-curl-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#7-start-the-rollout","content":"7\\. Start the rollout"},"3282":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"8\\. Play the device (DDI)"},"3283":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"9\\. Release the next batches"},"3284":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#10-check-the-result","content":"10\\. Check the result"},"3285":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"Things that behave differently"},"3286":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3287":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"3288":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"The same update as in the native guide, against the service in hawkBit mode. The management requests go to Lamassu Updates. The device side is a different protocol: devices poll hawkBit's DDI API, not this service and not WFX. The commands were run against a real hawkBit 1.1.0, and the responses are real, trimmed where long. Examples that say they were not run were checked against the code only."},"3289":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"The differences from native mode, in short:"},"3290":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Native"},"3291":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit"},"3292":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Build"},"3293":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Upload artifacts and a sw-description to the pack, then build the pack"},"3294":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Build a **module** in the catalog first, then create the pack from it"},"3295":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Pack after creation"},"3296":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"`draft`"},"3297":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Already `built`"},"3298":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Who tells the device"},"3299":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"WFX job"},"3300":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit action, read over DDI"},"3301":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Device reports to"},"3302":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"WFX"},"3303":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit (DDI feedback)"},"3304":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"Next batch, with `auto` on"},"3305":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"The service, from WFX events"},"3306":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","content":"hawkBit, from its rollout groups"},"3307":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"The stack is running in hawkBit mode: this service, its Postgres, hawkBit and the Lamassu device manager."},"3308":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"A device group in Lamassu with devices in it. This guide uses `fleet-a` with `dev-001` to `dev-004`."},"3309":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"`curl` and `jq`."},"3310":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"A SWU builder configured (`swugenerator_path`), to build a `swu-build` module. Without one, `POST .../build` on such a module answers `501`."},"3311":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#before-you-begin","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml` in the repository serves the API on port `10090`, like the native stack, so run one backend at a time on that port. `config-hawkbit-demo.yml` serves it on `10091`, which the repository's dashboard development setup points at for the hawkBit backend. Set `API` to wherever your instance listens. Through a Lamassu gateway the API is usually `https://lamassu.example.com/api/updates/v1` and each call needs your gateway credential, for example `-H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"`."},"3312":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#1-check-the-backend","content":"`artifact_encryption`, `software_module_composition`, `standalone_software_modules` and `software_module_replace` appear in that list too if the build settings or hawkBit's module types are missing. See Capabilities."},"3313":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#2-create-a-module-in-the-catalog","content":"A hawkBit distribution set can only link **built** modules, so the module comes first. `delivery_intent` says how it ships: `swu-build` builds a `.swu` from your files and a sw-description. See hawkBit mode for the other intents (`swu-prebuilt`, `raw`)."},"3314":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#2-create-a-module-in-the-catalog","content":"`type` is `os` or `application`, and `type`, `name` and `version` are required. Without a `delivery_intent` the module is `undecided`, which accepts files but cannot be built or linked until you choose one with `PUT /softwaremodules/by-id/$MID`."},"3315":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#3-upload-the-file-and-the-sw-description","content":"Use the same `index.html` and `sw-description` as in the native guide."},"3316":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#3-upload-the-file-and-the-sw-description","content":"A `swu-build` module refuses a finished `.swu` as input, and a `swu-prebuilt` module takes exactly one `.swu`."},"3317":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#4-build-the-module","content":"Building replaced the module's input files with the finished `.swu`. The build body is optional. To encrypt or sign, send `user`, `encryption_key_name`, `encryption_alg_name`, `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` and `signature_certificate`, as in the signing and encryption page. A module can be built once: to change it, release a new version of the module."},"3318":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#5-create-the-pack-from-the-built-module","content":"The pack is built from the start. Its `uri` is a hawkBit download address that devices resolve themselves. In hawkBit mode `modules` takes only `source_module_id` entries, and each module must be built and compatible with the pack's packaging. Several entries make a multi-module pack, and then `GET .../swu/download` answers `400`: download each module's deliverable with `GET .../modules/:moduleKey/artifact/download`."},"3319":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"A group's devices only exist in hawkBit once the service has registered them. The service does that whenever it lists the group's devices, which a launch, a dry run, a job listing or a compliance read all do. The canary check runs **before** that, so on the first launch of a group that has not been listed yet, a `test_device_id` fails:"},"3320":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"Run the dry run without a canary first. It registers the group's devices in hawkBit as targets and tags them `group:fleet-a`:"},"3321":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"`never_seen_devices` lists targets that have not contacted hawkBit yet. A rollout group cannot finish while its devices never poll, so check this list. `superseded_devices` lists devices that already have an update in flight: creating the launch **cancels** those actions, because hawkBit replaces a target's unfinished actions with the new one. Now create the launch with the canary:"},"3322":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"`workflow_type` has no WFX meaning here: `phased` makes a hawkBit `soft` action (the device decides when to install) and anything else a `forced` one. Define a helper to follow the launch:"},"3323":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#6-preview-the-launch-then-create-it","content":"To start the rollout later, add `scheduled_at` (RFC 3339) to the create body. hawkBit's own scheduler then starts it, and a `rollout` call before that time leaves the schedule alone. Not run here."},"3324":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#7-start-the-rollout","content":"The service started a hawkBit rollout: the canary in the first group and the rest after it."},"3325":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"A real device runs SWUpdate's `suricatta`, which does this itself. These are the requests it makes."},"3326":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"First, devices must authenticate. hawkBit's default is to refuse them. Enable security tokens for the tenant once, and read the target's token:"},"3327":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"This is the local setup. In a deployment where devices reach hawkBit through the Lamassu gateway, `hawkbit.ddi_url` is the gateway path (for example `https://lamassu.example.com/api/hawkbit-ddi`) and devices authenticate as the gateway requires, typically with their client certificate. See Connect a device."},"3328":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Poll. When there is work, the answer links to a `deploymentBase`:"},"3329":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Read the deployment and download its artifact:"},"3330":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"When the service publishes the device artifact URL (the `ddi_url` path), it serves that same route itself, for modules in the device's assigned or installed set only, and with S3 presigning enabled it answers `302` to a short-lived signed URL. A device does not need to know the difference: it follows the redirect."},"3331":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"Report progress and the result. `closed` with `finished: success` is the end:"},"3332":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"The service reads hawkBit when you ask, so the launch is up to date:"},"3333":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#8-play-the-device-ddi","content":"To report a failure, send `\"finished\":\"failure\"` in the `closed` feedback."},"3334":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"With `auto` off, hawkBit pauses after each group. Each `rollout` call releases the next one:"},"3335":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"Here a hawkBit action is shown as a workflow state: a scheduled action is `CREATED`, a running one `DOWNLOADING` (hawkBit does not report finer steps), a finished one (or one that finished with a warning) `ACTIVATED`, and a failed, cancelled or cancelling one `TERMINATED`. Repeat step 8 for `dev-002` and `dev-003` (the token comes from each target), then call `rollout` once more for `dev-004`. When every action is finished:"},"3336":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#9-release-the-next-batches","content":"hawkBit decides when a batch is finished. After the last device of a batch reports, hawkBit pauses the rollout, and for a moment its group still reads `running`. The service cannot tell that pause from one an operator made, so a `rollout` call in that window answers `400` with `rollout 1 is paused; resume it first`. Call `resume` and hawkBit releases the next batch itself:"},"3337":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Automatic rollout.** With `auto: true`, hawkBit advances the groups itself once `approval_threshold` is met. The service does not run an event consumer in this mode. The thresholds are set on every rollout group, and hawkBit evaluates both percentages **per group**, not against all devices as native does. An unset or `0` threshold becomes 100, so an unset `error_threshold` never trips. The canary group always needs 100%. They apply with `auto` off too."},"3338":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**A tripped error threshold.** hawkBit then pauses the rollout, and the service reports the launch as `cancelled`. `resume` and `rollout` both answer `400` for it."},"3339":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Pause and resume.** `pause` and `resume` map to hawkBit's rollout pause and resume, but only a pause an operator made can be resumed. hawkBit already holds the rollout between groups when `auto` is off, so `pause` then answers `400` (\"Rollout can only be paused in state running but current state is paused\") and `resume` answers `400` (\"not paused; use Execute to release the next batch\"). Use `rollout` to release the next group."},"3340":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Strategy read-back.** The strategy shown for a launch is derived from the hawkBit rollout's groups, not stored. A launch created with a fixed batch of 2 for 4 devices reads back as `percentage` 50."},"3341":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Static membership.** A rollout is built from the devices of the group when the launch is created. Devices added to the group later are not picked up (`launch_device_assignment` is unsupported)."},"3342":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#things-that-behave-differently","content":"**Not available.** Per-device encryption, custom workflows (`GET /workflows` returns an empty list), editing a running strategy, marking a launch complete, pushed job events (progress is polled), set-level prebuilt upload, and building a pack directly. `POST .../swu` answers `501`:"},"3343":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"3344":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"3345":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`501` building a module: no SWU builder"},"3346":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`swugenerator_path` is not configured. Configure it, or upload a prebuilt `.swu` with intent `swu-prebuilt`"},"3347":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`501` building a module: no SymKMS or no KMS endpoint"},"3348":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Encryption needs `symkms_endpoint` and signing needs `kms_endpoint`. Build without those fields, or configure them"},"3349":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... is not built` creating a pack"},"3350":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module linked into a pack must be built first. Build it in the catalog"},"3351":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... incompatible with distribution set packaging`"},"3352":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A `raw` module cannot go into a `swu` pack, and a `swu-prebuilt` module cannot go into a `non-swu` pack"},"3353":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... frozen` changing a module"},"3354":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module linked to a pack is frozen. Edit and build it in the catalog, then link it again"},"3355":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... already built`"},"3356":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A module is built once. Release a new version of the module"},"3357":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`409 ... being built or changed by another request`"},"3358":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Another request holds the module. Retry when it finishes"},"3359":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Creating a module answers `400` mentioning that hawkBit reserves the name and version"},"3360":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"hawkBit keeps the name and version of a module that was assigned to a device, even after it is deleted. Use a new version"},"3361":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The canary fails with `device ... does not exist`"},"3362":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The group's devices are not in hawkBit yet. Run a dry run without `test_device_id` first"},"3363":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A launch never advances"},"3364":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Check `never_seen_devices`: a device that never polls blocks its rollout group"},"3365":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#next-steps","content":"hawkBit mode for modules, delivery intents and what lives where"},"3366":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#next-steps","content":"Connect a device for the device-side setup"},"3367":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#next-steps","content":"API reference"},"3368":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/hawkbit-curl#next-steps","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3369":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"page","content":"Update flow with curl, native backend","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Updates","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl"},"3370":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","content":"Every request of a complete update in native mode, from creating a pack to the last device, with real responses."},"3371":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"3372":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#1-check-the-backend","content":"1\\. Check the backend"},"3373":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#2-create-the-pack","content":"2\\. Create the pack"},"3374":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#3-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"3\\. Upload the sw-description and the artifact"},"3375":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"4\\. Build the `.swu`"},"3376":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#5-preview-then-create-the-launch","content":"5\\. Preview, then create the launch"},"3377":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#6-roll-out-the-canary","content":"6\\. Roll out the canary"},"3378":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#7-play-the-device","content":"7\\. Play the device"},"3379":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#8-roll-out-the-rest","content":"8\\. Roll out the rest"},"3380":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#9-check-the-result","content":"9\\. Check the result"},"3381":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#variations","content":"Variations"},"3382":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#let-the-service-release-the-batches","content":"Let the service release the batches"},"3383":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#pause-resume-retry-and-cancel","content":"Pause, resume, retry and cancel"},"3384":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#schedule-a-launch","content":"Schedule a launch"},"3385":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#require-a-version-before-updating","content":"Require a version before updating"},"3386":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#update-one-device-to-a-version","content":"Update one device to a version"},"3387":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#a-new-version","content":"A new version"},"3388":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-with-a-shared-key","content":"Encrypt with a shared key"},"3389":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-per-device","content":"Encrypt per device"},"3390":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#sign-the-package","content":"Sign the package"},"3391":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3392":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"3393":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","content":"A complete update, request by request: create a pack, build it, send it to a group in batches, play the device, and follow progress. Every command was run against a native-mode stack, and the responses are real, trimmed where long, except where a section says it was not run: those examples were checked against the code only."},"3394":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","content":"If you use the hawkBit backend the flow differs, mainly in how a pack is built and how devices report. For the screens that do the same, see the dashboard guide."},"3395":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#before-you-begin","content":"The stack is running in native mode: the service, Postgres, WFX and the Lamassu device manager."},"3396":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#before-you-begin","content":"A device group exists in Lamassu with devices in it. This guide uses the group `fleet-a` with the devices `dev-001` to `dev-004`."},"3397":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#before-you-begin","content":"`curl` and `jq` are installed. `jq` is only used to pull values out of responses."},"3398":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#before-you-begin","content":"These are the addresses of the Docker Compose stack in the repository. Through a Lamassu gateway the API is usually `https://lamassu.example.com/api/updates/v1`, and every call then needs the credential your gateway requires, for example `-H \"Authorization: Bearer $TOKEN\"`. The service itself does no authentication. See Security."},"3399":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#2-create-the-pack","content":"The pack is `draft`. It stays editable until it is built. `name`, `version` (semver) and `group_id` are required; the name must be unique in the group, or the request answers `409`."},"3400":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#3-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"The sw-description tells SWUpdate what to install. This minimal one installs a web page. See the sw-description rules in Publish and roll out an update."},"3401":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#3-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"The artifact name is global: all packs share one catalog, and a name can only be reused with a **higher** `version`. Uploading `index.html` again as `1.0.0` fails with `version 1.0.0 must be greater than the current latest version`. A file named `.swu` or `.tar.gz` must really be one, or the upload answers `400`."},"3402":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"`selected_artifact_ids` is what puts artifacts into the build. Without it the build fails."},"3403":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"The `uri` starts with the service's `update_domain`. In the Compose stack that is `http://updates:10090/updates/v1/` (`config-docker.yml`), a name that resolves only inside the Compose network, because it is the address devices use. From your host, call the same path on `localhost:10090`, as the next command does."},"3404":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"The pack is now `built`: artifacts can no longer be added or linked to it. You can fetch the shared package (this one is not encrypted):"},"3405":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"Downloads support `Range` and `HEAD`, so a client can learn the size first and resume an interrupted transfer, for example with `curl -C - -o water.swu $P/swu/download`. With S3 storage and presigning enabled, the same request can answer `302` to a short-lived signed URL, which `curl -L` follows."},"3406":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#4-build-the-swu","content":"If the build fails, the pack gets the status `build_failed` and `last_build_error` holds the reason. It stays editable: fix the cause and build again."},"3407":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#5-preview-then-create-the-launch","content":"A dry run shows who would receive the update, without creating anything:"},"3408":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#5-preview-then-create-the-launch","content":"Create it. `test_device_id` is the canary: it goes alone first and must succeed before anyone else is touched. `rollout_value` 2 means batches of two devices."},"3409":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#5-preview-then-create-the-launch","content":"A small helper makes the launch easy to follow in the next steps:"},"3410":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#6-roll-out-the-canary","content":"An empty `status` means running. Only the canary is active. The service created one WFX job for `dev-001`:"},"3411":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#7-play-the-device","content":"A real device does this by itself. These commands are what it sends to WFX, so you can drive a test device by hand. First the device asks WFX for its job:"},"3412":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#7-play-the-device","content":"The device downloads the `uri`, installs it, and reports each step:"},"3413":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#7-play-the-device","content":"The `direct` workflow is `INSTALL → INSTALLING → INSTALLED → ACTIVATE → ACTIVATING → ACTIVATED`. WFX itself makes the `INSTALLED → ACTIVATE` step. To report a failure, move a job to `TERMINATED`."},"3414":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#7-play-the-device","content":"The service hears about every change from WFX through its event stream and updates the launch. This takes a moment, so if `status` still shows the device as active, run it again after a second:"},"3415":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#8-roll-out-the-rest","content":"The canary passed. Each `rollout` call now sends the next batch of two:"},"3416":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#8-roll-out-the-rest","content":"Walk those devices through steps like in step 7, then call `rollout` again for the last device. When nothing is pending or active the launch completes by itself:"},"3417":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#8-roll-out-the-rest","content":"`completed_count` counts only successes: a failed device is counted in `failed_count`. A launch is marked `completed` once nothing is pending or active, even if some devices failed, so check `failed_count` before you call the update a success."},"3418":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#9-check-the-result","content":"To track drift, declare the version devices should be on, then read compliance:"},"3419":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#9-check-the-result","content":"The fleet-wide view of the last attempt per device and pack, including attempts outside any launch, is one call. Not run here; the brackets of a filter need `curl -g`:"},"3420":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#let-the-service-release-the-batches","content":"With `auto` on, the service sends the next batch itself once enough of the current one succeeded. `approval_threshold` is the percentage of the batch that must succeed (0 or 100 mean all of it). `error_threshold` applies to every launch, `auto` or not: the launch is cancelled once the number of failed devices reaches that percentage of **all** devices, rounded up. With 4 devices at 75%, the third failure cancels it."},"3421":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#let-the-service-release-the-batches","content":"This example uses a second pack, `valve-panel`, created and built like `water-panel` (steps 2 to 4). Artifact names are global and a name that already exists must get a higher version, so give this one its own file name:"},"3422":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#let-the-service-release-the-batches","content":"Call `rollout` once to start. A second call is refused:"},"3423":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#let-the-service-release-the-batches","content":"If one device of the first batch fails (`TERMINATED`) and the other succeeds, 50% succeeded meets the threshold and the next batch is dispatched on its own."},"3424":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#pause-resume-retry-and-cancel","content":"A pause lets the batch in flight finish and holds the next one. `retry-failed` puts the failed devices back in the pending pool and releases the next batch. That batch is drawn at random from all pending devices, so it can also contain devices that were never sent, and if more devices failed than fit in a batch only one batch goes out. It answers `400` when nothing failed, and it re-opens a completed or cancelled launch (`\"status\":\"running\"`). A failed canary pauses the launch by itself, and `resume` then sends the canary again. A cancelled launch cannot be resumed, and in-flight devices finish their current job."},"3425":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#schedule-a-launch","content":"Not run here. `scheduled_at` (RFC 3339) delays the first batch. The service checks for due launches about every 30 seconds, so the start can be up to that late. A `rollout` call before the time does nothing."},"3426":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#schedule-a-launch","content":"The schedule survives a restart and runs on whichever replica currently holds the leader role, so a scheduled launch is dispatched once even with several replicas."},"3427":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#require-a-version-before-updating","content":"Not run here. A pack can require that a device already carries another pack, or a module, at a minimum version. The rule lives on the pack you launch. Devices that fail it are left out, and the dry run lists them:"},"3428":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#require-a-version-before-updating","content":"Each failure names the `device_id`, the `distribution_set_name` (and `module_key` for a module rule), the `current_version` the device has (empty if none) and the `required` constraint, for example `>=1.0.0`. Use `required_module_key` with a `type:name` value to require a module instead. `force_preconditions: true` in the launch body deploys to every device anyway and records the failures."},"3429":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#update-one-device-to-a-version","content":"Not run here. `force-version` launches a single device to an exact pack version, outside any campaign, and answers `202`. The device must be a member of the pack's group:"},"3430":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#update-one-device-to-a-version","content":"Without `workflow`, a `swu` pack uses `phased`. Only the pack's current version can be forced, unless the pack was created with `allow_previous_version_download`."},"3431":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#a-new-version","content":"The version must be higher than the current one, and the pack keeps its id. The new version starts as `draft`. The artifact links and the module composition carry over, but the sw-description does not: upload it again. Then build with `selected_artifact_ids` (a build replaces the carried links with the ones you select), after uploading a new artifact version if the file changed."},"3432":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-with-a-shared-key","content":"One key encrypts the `.swu` for every device. The sw-description must mark the files to encrypt with `encrypted = true;`. Use a separate pack for each encryption variant: a new version inherits the previous version's encryption settings, and a plain build does not clear them. Rebuilding an already built pack with other settings leaves stale fields too. See Limitations."},"3433":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-with-a-shared-key","content":"This helper creates a pack, uploads a sw-description that marks its file `encrypted = true;`, and uploads the artifact. It prints the artifact id."},"3434":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-with-a-shared-key","content":"The pack then reports `\"encryption_mode\":\"shared\"`. The device needs the same key and algorithm. See Signing and encryption."},"3435":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-per-device","content":"Each device gets its own package and key. This is another pack, built with the same helper. The sw-description must mark a file `encrypted = true;`, or the build is refused."},"3436":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-per-device","content":"If a device has no key at build time, the build still succeeds and the pack records the gap. If **no** device has a key, the build fails instead."},"3437":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-per-device","content":"A launch on that pack is refused, dry runs included, and `force_preconditions` does not override it:"},"3438":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#encrypt-per-device","content":"Coverage is recorded when the pack is built, so assigning the missing key is not enough. Build the pack again (a new version) with a key for every device."},"3439":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#sign-the-package","content":"Add the KMS signing fields to the build body. They need a signing key and certificate in the Lamassu KMS, with `kms_endpoint` and `sign_script_path` set. This request was not run here, because it needs a KMS. See Signing and encryption."},"3440":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Symptom"},"3441":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Cause and fix"},"3442":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`409` on `artifact/upload` or `artifact/link`"},"3443":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The pack version is already `built`. Create a new version with `POST .../new`"},"3444":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`409` on `POST .../distribution-sets`"},"3445":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"A pack with that name already exists in the group"},"3446":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 version ... must be greater than the current latest version`"},"3447":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"An artifact name is global and its version must increase. Upload with a higher `version`"},"3448":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The build fails with an empty binaries directory"},"3449":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The build received no `selected_artifact_ids`"},"3450":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400` creating a launch: pack has not been built"},"3451":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Build it first. A pack in `build_failed` is not launchable either"},"3452":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`400 ... is per-device encrypted and only N of M devices have a package`"},"3453":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Some devices have no `firmware-encryption` key. Assign keys and build a new version"},"3454":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`rollout` answers `400` with `rolls out automatically`"},"3455":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The launch has `auto` on and already started. Wait for the approval threshold, or pause it"},"3456":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`rollout` answers `400` with `test device ... failed`"},"3457":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The canary failed. Resume the launch to retry it, or cancel"},"3458":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`413` on an upload"},"3459":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"The file is over `max_artifact_size_mb` (10 GiB by default), or the gateway or ingress limit in front of the service is lower"},"3460":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"`501` on a module route"},"3461":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#troubleshooting","content":"Native mode has no per-module deliverables. Build the pack instead"},"3462":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#next-steps","content":"Update flow with curl, hawkBit backend"},"3463":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#next-steps","content":"Connect a device for what a real device must implement"},"3464":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#next-steps","content":"API reference"},"3465":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/native-curl#next-steps","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3466":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"page","content":"Publish and roll out an update","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Updates","Guides"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out"},"3467":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","content":"Create an update pack, attach an artifact, build the deliverable and roll it out to a device group in batches."},"3468":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"Before you begin"},"3469":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"1\\. Create the pack"},"3470":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"2\\. Upload the sw-description and the artifact"},"3471":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#compose-a-pack-from-several-modules-optional","content":"Compose a pack from several modules (optional)"},"3472":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"3\\. Build the deliverable"},"3473":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"4\\. Create the launch"},"3474":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"5\\. Roll it out"},"3475":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#verify-the-result","content":"Verify the result"},"3476":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#ship-the-next-version","content":"Ship the next version"},"3477":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit mode"},"3478":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#troubleshooting","content":"Troubleshooting"},"3479":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#next-steps","content":"Next steps"},"3480":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","content":"This guide takes one update from nothing to devices: create an update pack, attach an artifact and a `sw-description`, build the deliverable, create a launch (a campaign in the dashboard) and release it batch by batch. The requests use native mode. hawkBit mode builds and creates packs in a different order, described in hawkBit mode. To do the same through screens, follow Use the dashboard."},"3481":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"The stack is running and `curl localhost:10090/health` answers."},"3482":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"A Lamassu IoT device group that contains the devices you want to update. Its ID is `$GROUP`. A pack belongs to one group and can only be launched to that group's devices."},"3483":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"The binary to deliver and, for an SWU pack, a `sw-description` file."},"3484":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"Devices that can receive the update. See Connect a device."},"3485":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#before-you-begin","content":"The service has no built-in authentication, so these examples send none. Put a gateway that authenticates callers in front of it: see Security."},"3486":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"The response is `201` with the pack, including its `id`. A pack starts as `draft`."},"3487":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Field"},"3488":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Notes"},"3489":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`name`"},"3490":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Required. Unique within the group; a duplicate answers `409`. Native mode uses it as a path segment, so it may contain only letters, digits, `.`, `_` and `-` (no spaces)"},"3491":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`version`"},"3492":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Required. Strict semver `x.y.z`, set by you"},"3493":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`group_id`"},"3494":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Required in the body. Use the same value as in the path"},"3495":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`type`"},"3496":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`rawfile` or `firmware`. Recorded on the pack and sent to the device in the job; the dashboard also offers `both` and `other`. Not validated at creation"},"3497":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`packaging`"},"3498":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`swu` (default) or `non-swu`. A `non-swu` pack delivers its files as a `.tar.gz` and uses the `download-install` workflow"},"3499":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`allow_previous_version_download`"},"3500":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Optional. Lets devices download older versions of the pack"},"3501":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`preconditions`"},"3502":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"Optional rules a device must meet to receive the pack. See Concepts"},"3503":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"`modules`"},"3504":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#1-create-the-pack","content":"**hawkBit mode only**: the pack's composition, as built catalog modules. Native ignores it"},"3505":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"The `sw-description` is an SWUpdate file that lists what the device installs. Its format is SWUpdate's, and the SWUpdate documentation is the reference. When the service builds the `.swu`, `swugenerator` reads this file and the staged binaries, so the `filename` of every image must be the name of an uploaded file. A minimal one:"},"3506":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"`swugenerator` fills in the final `filename` (with `.zlib` added, and `.enc` for encrypted files), the `sha256` and, for encrypted files, the `ivt` property. For an encrypted build, add `encrypted = true;` to each image that must be encrypted. Two rules cause most failures:"},"3507":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"`encrypted = true` must appear only in a build that supplies a key (the build fails without one), and a per-device build refuses a description in which no image has it."},"3508":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"Compressed images need `decompressed-size`."},"3509":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"If you build the `.swu` yourself and upload it as a prebuilt deliverable, you fill in `sha256` and `ivt` yourself, and the `sha256` is over the bytes the device downloads, because SWUpdate hashes before it decrypts."},"3510":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"`artifact_name` defaults to the file name without its extension. `version` is optional; when you upload a new file under an existing `artifact_name` it must be strictly higher than the highest version already stored under that name."},"3511":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"The artifact is stored as a global artifact and linked to this pack. The response contains its `id`. To reuse an artifact that is already uploaded, link it with `POST .../artifact/link` and `{\"artifact_id\":\"<id>\"}`."},"3512":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"The largest accepted file is `max_artifact_size_mb` (10 GiB by default). A bigger upload answers `413`."},"3513":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#2-upload-the-sw-description-and-the-artifact","content":"Once the pack is built, uploads and links answer `409`: create a new version first."},"3514":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#compose-a-pack-from-several-modules-optional","content":"A native pack is a composition of software modules: one `os` module plus any number of `application` modules. A pack with no declared modules behaves as a single implicit `os` module that owns the artifacts you uploaded above. To add an application module and give it its own files:"},"3515":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#compose-a-pack-from-several-modules-optional","content":"The module key is `<type>:<name>`. Native still builds one `.swu` for the whole pack, from every module's artifacts and the pack's single `sw-description`. You can also compose from a module that already exists with `POST .../modules/import`; in native mode that copies the module, while in hawkBit mode it links the same module. See Concepts for the model."},"3516":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"`selected_artifact_ids` is what puts artifacts into the build: only the listed artifacts are staged. With an empty list the build fails because no binaries were staged, and the pack becomes `build_failed`. Take the ID from the artifact upload response, or from `GET $API/artifacts`."},"3517":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"The body above builds an unencrypted, unsigned `.swu`. To sign or encrypt, add fields as described in Signing and encryption."},"3518":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"For a `non-swu` pack, call `POST .../package` instead of `.../swu`. With no `selected_artifact_ids` it packages the artifacts linked to the pack."},"3519":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"To deliver a file you built elsewhere, upload it to `POST .../swu/upload` (or `.../package/upload`) as a multipart `file`. It is stored and served unchanged, so it must already be signed and encrypted the way your devices expect. Native mode only."},"3520":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#3-build-the-deliverable","content":"When the build succeeds, the pack becomes `built` and its artifacts and composition are immutable. If it fails, the pack becomes `build_failed` and `last_build_error` holds the reason: fix the input and build again. A build that runs while another one holds the same pack answers `409`."},"3521":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"The launch targets every device of the group at the moment you create it, and it needs a built pack. The response is `201` with `launch_id`, `precondition_failures`, `forced`, and, in hawkBit mode, `superseded_devices` and `never_seen_devices`."},"3522":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Field"},"3523":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Notes"},"3524":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`distribution_set_name`, `workflow_type`, `rollout_type`, `rollout_value`"},"3525":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Required. `rollout_value` must be greater than 0"},"3526":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`rollout_type`"},"3527":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`percentage` of the group per batch, or `fixed` (a device count). Any value other than `percentage` is read as a count"},"3528":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`workflow_type`"},"3529":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Native: `direct`, `phased`, `download-install`, or the full name of another workflow registered in WFX (`GET $API/workflows`). hawkBit: `phased` creates a soft action, anything else a forced one"},"3530":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`test_device_id`"},"3531":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Optional canary: a member of the group that is updated first and must succeed before any other device is touched"},"3532":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`auto`, `approval_threshold`, `error_threshold`"},"3533":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Optional. `auto` releases later batches by itself. Both thresholds are percentages from 0 to 100"},"3534":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`scheduled_at`"},"3535":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Optional RFC 3339 time. The first batch is delayed until then"},"3536":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`name`, `description`, `weight`"},"3537":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Optional. `name` defaults to the pack's name. `weight` (0 to 1000) is stored but nothing reads it"},"3538":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"`force_preconditions`"},"3539":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Deploy to devices that fail the pack's preconditions anyway. The failures are still recorded"},"3540":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Choose the workflow to match the pack:"},"3541":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Use `direct` for SWU packs unless you drive WFX yourself. The `phased` workflow has steps that WFX or an operator must confirm, and this service does not advance them. A `phased` launch stays at its first state until someone confirms it through WFX."},"3542":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"For a `non-swu` pack set `workflow_type` to `download-install`. The launch uses the value you give verbatim, so `direct` would run the SWU workflow and the update would look stuck after the device finished."},"3543":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"In hawkBit mode there is no WFX. The choice is hawkBit's install mode."},"3544":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"If the pack has preconditions, preview who qualifies before creating anything by adding `?dry_run=true` to the same request. It answers `200` with `qualifying_devices`, `precondition_failures`, `superseded_devices` and `never_seen_devices`, and creates nothing."},"3545":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"**Approval and error thresholds.** With `auto: true`, the next batch is released once at least `approval_threshold` percent of the current batch has succeeded (0 means the whole batch). In native mode the campaign is cancelled when `error_threshold` percent of all its devices have failed; in hawkBit mode it stops when more than that percentage of a batch fails. A failed canary pauses a native campaign instead: resume it to retry the canary."},"3546":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#4-create-the-launch","content":"Take the launch ID from the response. It is `$LAUNCH` below."},"3547":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Without `auto`, each call dispatches the next batch (the canary first, if you set one). With `auto: true`, call it once to start the first batch: the service then releases the later batches itself as the approval threshold is met, and further calls answer `400`. If the launch has a future `scheduled_at`, the call is accepted but does nothing: the service starts it by itself at that time (native checks every 30 seconds; hawkBit's own scheduler starts the rollout)."},"3548":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"A native launch moves through these statuses:"},"3549":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"You can steer a launch while it runs:"},"3550":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Action"},"3551":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Request"},"3552":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Effect"},"3553":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Pause"},"3554":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"`POST $API/groups/$GROUP/launch/$LAUNCH/pause`"},"3555":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"No further batches until resumed. Devices already in flight finish"},"3556":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Resume"},"3557":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"`POST .../resume`"},"3558":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Native: an automatic campaign releases its next batch at once if the current one already met the threshold, and resuming after a failed canary retries it"},"3559":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Retry failed devices"},"3560":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"`POST .../retry-failed`"},"3561":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Re-queues the failed devices and dispatches them. Answers `400` when there is none"},"3562":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Cancel (terminal)"},"3563":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"`POST .../cancel`"},"3564":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Pending devices are not updated"},"3565":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Mark complete (terminal)"},"3566":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"`POST .../complete`"},"3567":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/guides/publish-and-roll-out#5-roll-it-out","content":"Not available in