ontent":"`sync-to-latest` takes an optional body with `groupID` (also accepted as `?groupID=`), `distribution_set_ids` to limit the packs and `workflow`. If some devices could not be dispatched it answers `207`, or `400` when none were, with `{\"err\": \"...\", \"drift\": {...}}`."},"4572":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-561","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"`force-version` takes `distribution_set_id` and `version` (required), `group_id` and `workflow`. The device must be a member of the pack's group. For a `swu` pack `workflow` defaults to `phased`, and for a `non-swu` pack to `download-install`. Native mode accepts only the pack's current version unless the pack has `allow_previous_version_download`, and `sync-to-latest` has the same limit. hawkBit mode ignores `workflow` in both routes."},"4573":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-562","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#version-compliance-and-latest-versions","content":"A drift entry has `distribution_set_id`, `distribution_set_name`, `current_version`, `latest_version`, `in_sync` and `missing`. A `version-status` row has `device_id`, `distribution_set_id`, `distribution_set_name`, `current_version`, `latest_version`, `in_sync` and, when newer than the declared one, `newest_version`."},"4574":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api-563","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/api#device-artifact-download-hawkbit-mode","content":"In hawkBit mode the service also serves hawkBit's device artifact URL, so a gateway can publish it on the same host as the rest 