dates/reference/capabilities-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Conditional"},"4717":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"`software_module_replace`: swap a module for another version of itself"},"4718":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"**No**"},"4719":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#per-backend-support","content":"Conditional"},"4720":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`artifact_encryption`** is reported unsupported only when none of `swugenerator_path`, `symkms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` is configured. Each build option still needs its own settings: see Signing and encryption."},"4721":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`software_module_composition`, `standalone_software_modules` and `software_module_replace`** depend on the hawkBit server having the pre-seeded `os` and `application` module types and the `os_app` or `app` set type. The service probes this with a 5 second timeout, caches the result for about five minutes and assumes support when hawkBit is unreachable. When the probe fails, all three flags are reported unsupported together."},"4722":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`software_module_deliverables`** is always reported supported in hawkBit mode. Building a `swu-build` module still needs a `swugenerator_path`, and without one the build answers `501`."},"4723":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#conditional-flags-in-hawkbit-mode","content":"**`prebuilt_deliverable`**: a hawkBit pack is never built directly. A `swu-prebuilt` catalog module accepts a finished `.swu` instead."},"4724":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#flags-that-differ-in-meaning","content":"Both backends report `software_module_composition`, but importing a module **links** it in hawkBit mode (both packs share one module) and **copies** it in native mode. The reusable-modules list reports this per candidate in its `shared` field, so a client can tell the operator which one they get. See Concepts."},"4725":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#flags-that-differ-in-meaning","content":"In native mode a launch dispatches one job per device with a single download URI, so a module has no deliverable of its own: the pack builds one `.swu` from every module's inputs. That is why `software_module_deliverables` and `software_module_replace` are unsupported there."},"4726":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Call `capabilities` once at start-up and before showing a feature the table marks as backend-dependent."},"4727":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Treat a `501` on a route as authoritative: hide the action instead of retrying."},"4728":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Do not infer the backend from the URL. Both serve the same `/updates/v1` routes; see the API reference for which routes answer `501` in which backend."},"4729":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#what-a-client-should-do","content":"Re-read the capabilities after changing hawkBit's module types or the build configuration."},"4730":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#next-steps","content":"API reference"},"4731":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/capabilities#next-steps","content":"hawkBit mode"},"4732":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"page","content":"Configuration reference","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Updates","Reference"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration"},"4733":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","content":"Every configuration key of Lamassu Updates, its default, which backend reads it, and how to override it with environment variables."},"4734":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"How the configuration is loaded"},"4735":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#which-keys-each-mode-reads","content":"Which keys each mode reads"},"4736":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#general-and-server-settings","content":"General and server settings"},"4737":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#database","content":"Database"},"4738":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Endpoints of other services"},"4739":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Build and signing"},"4740":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Upload limits"},"4741":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#blob-storage-blocks","content":"Blob storage blocks"},"4742":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#storage-storage","content":"Storage (`*.storage`)"},"4743":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"At-rest encryption (`*.encryption`)"},"4744":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Presigned downloads (`*.presign`)"},"4745":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit` block"},"4746":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Environment variables"},"4747":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"Minimal configurations"},"4748":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#symkms-as-its-own-process","content":"SymKMS as its own process"},"4749":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#related-pages","content":"Related pages"},"4750":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","content":"Lamassu Updates reads a single YAML file at start-up. This page lists every key the code reads, its default, and which backend (`native` or `hawkbit`) uses it. Keys that appear in the example files but are not read are listed separately so you do not rely on them."},"4751":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"Set the file location with the `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` environment variable. If it is unset, the service reads `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml`, which is where the Docker image and the Helm chart mount it."},"4752":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"If `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` names a file that cannot be loaded (missing, or invalid YAML), the service logs a warning and &#x2A;*falls back to `/etc/lamassuiot/config.yml`**. In the Docker image that path holds the repository's developer `config.yml`, so a typo in the path can start the service with the wrong settings. If the fallback fails too, the service exits."},"4753":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"The file is read once. Restart the service after any change."},"4754":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"`LAMASSU_CONFIG_FILE`, which the Dockerfile and the Helm chart set, is not read by the code. Only `OTA_CONFIG_FILE` matters."},"4755":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"Any key can be overridden by an environment variable. See Environment variables."},"4756":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"The repository ships three examples:"},"4757":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"File"},"4758":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"For"},"4759":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"`config.yml`"},"4760":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"Local development in `native` mode"},"4761":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"`config-docker.yml`"},"4762":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"The `updates` container of `docker-compose.yml`"},"4763":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"`config-hawkbit.yml`"},"4764":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"Local development in `hawkbit` mode against the hawkBit of the compose file (host port 8090)"},"4765":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#how-the-configuration-is-loaded","content":"The examples contain values for one developer machine (absolute paths and LAN addresses) and development secrets. Replace all of them, and never reuse their keys or passwords."},"4766":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#which-keys-each-mode-reads","content":"Key"},"4767":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#which-keys-each-mode-reads","content":"`native`"},"4768":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#which-keys-each-mode-reads","content":"`hawkbit`"},"4769":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#which-keys-each-mode-reads","content":"`mode`, `app.*`, `storage.*`"},"4770":{"id":"/docs/pr-p