configuration#database","content":"`info`"},"4852":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#database","content":"Log level of the database layer. SQL statements are logged at `trace`."},"4853":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#database","content":"The database name is fixed to &#x2A;*`updates`**. There is no key for it. The service creates its tables and migrates them at start-up, but it does not create the database: create `updates` first. In Docker Compose, `init.sql` creates `updates` and `hawkbit`, and `POSTGRES_DB` creates `wfx`."},"4854":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-121","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#database","content":"The connection uses `sslmode=disable`. There is no way to enable TLS towards Postgres from the configuration. Keep the database on a private network."},"4855":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-122","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#database","content":"Each process keeps at most 25 open and 10 idle connections (connections are recycled after 30 minutes, or 5 idle minutes). Budget `25 x replicas` against the `max_connections` of Postgres."},"4856":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-123","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Key"},"4857":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-124","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Default"},"4858":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-125","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Mode"},"4859":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-126","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Description"},"4860":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-127","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`dms_endpoint`"},"4861":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-128","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"none"},"4862":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-129","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Required in `native`, optional in `hawkbit`"},"4863":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-130","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Base URL of the Lamassu Device Manager API, for example `http://host:8080/api/devmanager`. It is the source of device groups. Without it in `hawkbit` mode, groups are read from the `group:<id>` tags of the hawkBit targets. The service sends `X-Principal-ID: admin-mode` on these calls."},"4864":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-131","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`kms_endpoint`"},"4865":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-132","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"none"},"4866":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-133","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Both"},"4867":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-134","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Base URL of the Lamassu KMS API, for example `http://host:8080/api/kms/v1`. Needed to sign. See Signing and encryption."},"4868":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-135","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`symkms_endpoint`"},"4869":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-136","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"none"},"4870":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-137","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Both"},"4871":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-138","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Base URL of SymKMS, **without** the `/symkms/v1` path. In the monolith it points at the service itself (for example `http://localhost:10090`) and must match `app.server.port`. Empty means encryption is refused."},"4872":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-139","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`wfx_endpoint`"},"4873":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-140","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"none"},"4874":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-141","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`native`"},"4875":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-142","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Base URL of the WFX **management** API (port `8081` inside the Compose network, `9081` on the host). The service appends `/api/wfx/v1/`. Startup fails if WFX cannot be reached. Devices use the WFX client port instead."},"4876":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-143","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`update_domain`"},"4877":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-144","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"none"},"4878":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-145","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"`native`"},"4879":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-146","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#endpoints-of-other-services","content":"Public base URL devices use to download builds, for example `http://updates:10090/updates/v1/`. It **must end in `/updates/v1/`, with the trailing slash**: the service appends `groups/...` directly and stores the result as the pack URI. It must be reachable from the devices."},"4880":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-147","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Key"},"4881":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-148","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Default"},"4882":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-149","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Mode"},"4883":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-150","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Description"},"4884":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-151","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`swugenerator_path`"},"4885":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-152","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`swugenerator` on the `PATH` in `native`; unset in `hawkbit`"},"4886":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-153","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Both"},"4887":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-154","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Path to the `swugenerator` binary. In `hawkbit` mode the SWU builder exists only when this is set: without it, `swu-build` modules cannot be built (`501`). Raw-module builds do not need it."},"4888":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-155","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`sign_script_path`"},"4889":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-156","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"none"},"4890":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-157","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Both"},"4891":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-158","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"The signer script swugenerator calls for `.swu` signing, `sign_kms.sh` (`/app/sign_kms.sh` in the image). Signing a `.swu` needs this and `kms_endpoint`; the service refuses a signing request when either is missing."},"4892":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-159","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`workflow_file`"},"4893":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-160","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`wfx.workflow.dau.direct.yml` (relative to the working directory)"},"4894":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-161","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`native`"},"4895":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-162","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Path of the `direct` WFX workflow. The name &#x2A;*must contain `direct`**: the `phased`, `download-install` and `simple` files are found by replacing that word in the path, and startup fails otherwise. The service uploads the workflows missing in WFX at start-up."},"4896":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-163","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`update_files_base_dir`"},"4897":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-164","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"none"},"4898":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-165","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`native`"},"4899":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-166","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Base directory for build scratch (`in/`) and, until builds are published to the `builds` store, build outputs (`out/`). It also supplies the default `local_dir` of `artifacts` and `builds`."},"4900":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-167","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`sym_keys_dir`"},"4901":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-168","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"none"},"4902":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-169","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Both"},"4903":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-170","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Fallback directory for SymKMS key storage when `symkms.storage.local_dir` is empty."},"4904":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-171","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`build_memory_limit_mb`"},"4905":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-172","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`0` (no check)"},"4906":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-173","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"`hawkbit`"},"4907":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-174","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#build-and-signing","content":"Refuses a build that would encrypt a file in memory (about twice its size) above this limit, in MiB, before the process is killed for lack of memory."},"4908":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-175","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Key"},"4909":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-176","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Type"},"4910":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-177","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Default"},"4911":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-178","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Description"},"4912":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-179","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"`max_artifact_size_mb`"},"4913":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-180","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"integer"},"4914":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-181","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"`10240` (10 GiB)"},"4915":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-182","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Largest single uploaded file in MiB: artifact or prebuilt `.swu`. A larger multipart file gets `413` with the message `file \"<name>\" is <n> MiB; the maximum upload size is <m> MiB`. The HTTP body limit is this value plus 1 MiB. Values of `0` or less mean the default."},"4916":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-183","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#upload-limits","content":"Uploads are streamed: memory does not grow with the file, but each in-flight upload is written to a temporary file under `TMPDIR` (default `/tmp`) first, so it needs that much free disk. Any proxy in front of the service must accept the same size and keep the connection open: read and write timeouts are 6 hours and idle connections are closed after 5 minutes. See Operations."},"4917":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-184","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#blob-storage-blocks","content":"Four blocks share one layout, so artifacts, build outputs and key material can each live on local disk or in S3:"},"4918":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-185","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#blob-storage-blocks","content":"Block"},"4919":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-186","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#blob-storage-blocks","content":"Mode"},"4920":{"id":"/docs/pr-p