n-encryption","content":"none"},"4977":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-244","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"Required for `local`: a hex-encoded 32-byte key."},"4978":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-245","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"`awskms_key_id`"},"4979":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-246","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"none"},"4980":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-247","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"Required for `awskms`: key ARN or alias."},"4981":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-248","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"`awskms_region`"},"4982":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-249","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"`us-east-1`"},"4983":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-250","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"Region of the AWS KMS key."},"4984":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-251","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#at-rest-encryption-encryption","content":"An encrypted object is encrypted and decrypted whole, in memory: with at-rest encryption, reading or writing a 10 GiB artifact needs that much memory, and byte ranges are cut from the decrypted copy. A store with encryption enabled cannot use presigned downloads. For large files, prefer encrypting at the store (for example S3 server-side encryption) instead."},"4985":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-252","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"With S3 storage, a download can be answered with `302` to a short-lived signed URL of the store instead of streaming the bytes through the service. The caller is authorized first, as for any download. Native mode signs build outputs (`builds.presign`); `hawkbit` mode signs the objects of hawkBit's S3 plugin (`hawkbit.artifact_store.presign`). Artifact downloads by ID in `native` mode are always streamed."},"4986":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-253","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Key"},"4987":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-254","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Default"},"4988":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-255","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Description"},"4989":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-256","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`enabled`"},"4990":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-257","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`false`"},"4991":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-258","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Turns the feature on."},"4992":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-259","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`public_endpoint`"},"4993":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-260","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"the storage `s3_endpoint`"},"4994":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-261","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"Origin of the store **as devices reach it**, without a path (for example the gateway that publishes the bucket). It is what gets signed: the signature covers the `Host` header, so a URL signed for an in-cluster address is refused when a device fetches it through the gateway. Required unless devices reach the store at its own endpoint (for example AWS S3)."},"4995":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-262","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`ttl`"},"4996":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-263","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`60s`"},"4997":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-264","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"How long a URL can **start** a download. Between `1s` and 7 days. A transfer already under way is not cut when it expires."},"4998":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-265","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`min_remaining`"},"4999":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-266","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`min(25s, ttl/2)`"},"5000":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-267","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"A URL already signed for the same object is handed out again while it has at least this much validity left, so a retry or resume never gets a URL about to expire. Negative signs a fresh URL on every request. Must be lower than `ttl`."},"5001":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-268","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"`access_key_id`, `secret_access_key` (or the `_file` variants)"},"5002":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-269","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"none"},"5003":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-270","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"The credential that signs. &#x2A;*Required, and it must be a read-only credential different from the storage one.**"},"5004":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-271","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#presigned-downloads-presign","content":"At start-up the service refuses to run when the signing credential is the storage credential, when it can write to the bucket (it probes with a write), when the store rejects it (it waits up to 2 minutes for the store to accept it), or when `encryption.type` is not `none` (devices would receive ciphertext). If the store cannot be asked at all, it logs a warning and continues. The device must still be able to resolve and reach `public_endpoint`. See Security."},"5005":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-272","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Used only when `mode: hawkbit`."},"5006":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-273","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Key"},"5007":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-274","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Default"},"5008":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-275","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Description"},"5009":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-276","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.base_url`"},"5010":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-277","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"none (required)"},"5011":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-278","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"hawkBit Management API root, for example `http://hawkbit:8080`. Startup fails if it is empty. Calls time out after 30 s; artifact transfers after 6 h."},"5012":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-279","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.username`, `hawkbit.password`"},"5013":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-280","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"none"},"5014":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-281","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Management API Basic Auth credentials."},"5015":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-282","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.tenant`"},"5016":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-283","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`DEFAULT`"},"5017":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-284","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"DDI tenant path segment."},"5018":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-285","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.ddi_url`"},"5019":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-286","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.base_url`"},"5020":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-287","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"hawkBit's DDI root **as devices reach it** (for example `https://updates.example.com/api/hawkbit-ddi`). It is used to build the download URLs devices receive, and its path becomes the prefix of the DDI download route this service serves."},"5021":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-288","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"`hawkbit.artifact_store`"},"5022":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-289","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"none"},"5023":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-290","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"Same shape as the blob storage blocks: `storage` must point to the bucket and `s3_prefix` of hawkBit's S3 artifact plugin, and `presign` enables signed downloads. Without it, artifacts are streamed through hawkBit."},"5024":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-291","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#hawkbit-block","content":"The `storage` (Postgres) block is also required in `hawkbit` mode."},"5025":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-292","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Any key of the file can be overridden by an environment variable: the name is the key path in upper case with dots replaced by underscores. `KMS_ENDPOINT` overrides `kms_endpoint`, `STORAGE_PASSWORD` overrides `storage.password` and `BUILDS_PRESIGN_TTL` overrides `builds.presign.ttl`. The key must exist in the file (an empty value is enough): the loader only considers keys it has read from it."},"5026":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-293","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Variables the code reads besides these overrides:"},"5027":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-294","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Variable"},"5028":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-295","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Description"},"5029":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-296","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`OTA_CONFIG_FILE`"},"5030":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-297","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Configuration file path."},"5031":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-298","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`POD_NAME`, `POD_NAMESPACE`"},"5032":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-299","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Identity and namespace for Kubernetes leader election. The Helm chart sets them. If unset, the hostname and the service-account namespace file are used."},"5033":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-300","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`TMPDIR`"},"5034":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-301","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Where uploads and builds write temporary files (Go's temporary directory)."},"5035":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-302","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`SERVER_PORT`"},"5036":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-303","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"Used only by the health check of the Docker image to find the port. Default `10090`."},"5037":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-304","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"`AWS_*`"},"5038":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-305","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"The AWS default credential chain, when an S3 or AWS KMS block has no explicit credential."},"5039":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-306","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"For Docker Compose, the `.env` file is read by `docker-compose.yml`, not by the service: `HOST_IP`, `HAWKBIT_ADMIN_PASSWORD`, `HAWKBIT_ARTIFACT_STORAGE` and the `HAWKBIT_ARTIFACT_S3_*` and `LOCAL_S3_*` variables. See `.env.example` in the repository."},"5040":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-307","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#environment-variables","content":"With `app.logs.level: debug`, the service writes the whole loaded configuration to the log at start-up, including `storage.password`, `encryption.local_key`, S3 keys and `hawkbit.password`. In `native` mode the `storage` block, password included, is also printed to standard output at every start, whatever the log level. Use `info` or higher anywhere logs are stored or shared, and keep secrets in a secret store, not in the file (see the `*_file` credentials above)."},"5041":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-308","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"`native` mode needs the database, the endpoints it calls and storage paths. Start from `config-docker.yml`:"},"5042":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-309","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"`hawkbit` mode needs `mode: hawkbit`, `hawkbit.base_url`, the Management API credentials and the `storage` block. Add the build settings only if you want builds. The keys below are the ones `config-hawkbit.yml` uses:"},"5043":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-310","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#minimal-configurations","content":"In `hawkbit` mode the SymKMS routes are registered only when `symkms.storage.type` or `sym_keys_dir` is set. With `symkms_endpoint` set but neither of those, every key lookup would be answered `404` by the service itself."},"5044":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-311","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#symkms-as-its-own-process","content":"The `cmd/symkms` binary runs SymKMS alone. Its configuration has only `app` (as above), `symkms` (a storage block) and `sym_keys_dir`. Its key directory defaults to `/data/symmetric_keys` when neither `symkms.storage.local_dir` nor `sym_keys_dir` is set. It serves `/symkms/v1/*` but no `/health` route, and it has the same lack of authentication as the monolith: see Security."},"5045":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-312","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#related-pages","content":"Operations for the Helm values, scaling and backups."},"5046":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-313","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#related-pages","content":"hawkBit mode for what changes in that backend."},"5047":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-314","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#related-pages","content":"Signing and encryption for the keys behind `kms_endpoint` and `symkms`."},"5048":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration-315","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/reference/configuration#related-pages","content":"Troubleshooting for start-up errors."},"5049":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"page","content":"Security","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Updates","Operate"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security"},"5050":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","content":"What Lamassu Updates does and does not protect, and what to put around it before exposing it."},"5051":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Summary"},"5052":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"What to put in front of it"},"5053":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#how-the-service-identifies-itself-to-others","content":"How the service identifies itself to others"},"5054":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Routes to restrict"},"5055":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"What the service checks"},"5056":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"Presigned download URLs"},"5057":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Outbound connections"},"5058":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"Secrets"},"5059":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit mode"},"5060":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#request-limits","content":"Request limits"},"5061":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","content":"Lamassu Updates delegates authentication, authorization and TLS to the platform gateway in front of it. This page lists what the service itself enforces, what it does not, and what to configure around it. Read it before exposing the service beyond a trusted network."},"5062":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Area"},"5063":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"State"},"5064":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Authentication of API callers"},"5065":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**None in the service.** Every route is open to anyone who can reach the port. The gateway must authenticate."},"5066":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Authorization"},"5067":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**No roles or per-group permissions.** The service only does structural checks (see What the service checks). The gateway must authorize."},"5068":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"TLS and mTLS (inbound)"},"5069":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"**Not implemented.** The service always serves plain HTTP."},"5070":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"TLS to other systems"},"5071":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Postgres: always `sslmode=disable`. KMS: not verified in `native` mode, and the SWU signer script uses `curl -k`. See Outbound connections."},"5072":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"CORS"},"5073":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Any origin and any header are allowed."},"5074":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Rate limiting, security headers"},"5075":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"None added by the service."},"5076":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Package signing"},"5077":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available, through the Lamassu KMS. See Signing and encryption."},"5078":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Package encryption"},"5079":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available: shared key or per-device key."},"5080":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"At-rest encryption"},"5081":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"Available for artifacts, builds and keys, through the `encryption` block of each storage block."},"5082":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#summary","content":"The `cert_file`, `key_file` and `authentication.mutual_tls.*` keys exist in the configuration structs but are not read, so setting them does nothing."},"5083":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"Run the service behind a gateway or reverse proxy that:"},"5084":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Terminates TLS** between clients and the service."},"5085":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Authenticates and authorizes** callers: operators for the API, and devices for the download routes. A device must only reach its own download paths, so match the device certificate to the `:deviceID` (or `:controllerId`) in the path."},"5086":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"**Restricts the dangerous routes** to the callers that need them (see below)."},"5087":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"Keep the service on a private network. Devices need to reach only the download routes and, in `native` mode, the WFX **client** listener. In `hawkbit` mode they talk to hawkBit (and to the signed-URL store) and not to this service, except for the artifact download route described in hawkBit mode."},"5088":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-to-put-in-front-of-it","content":"WFX has a client listener (`8080` in Compose, published as `9080`) and a management listener (`8081`, published as `9081`). Lamassu Updates authenticates neither. Devices need the client listener only: do not expose the management port to devices or untrusted networks."},"5089":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#how-the-service-identifies-itself-to-others","content":"The service does not forward the caller's identity. Calls to the Lamassu Device Manager and the KMS carry the fixed header `X-Principal-ID: admin-mode`, which the platform's authorization layer accepts for internal callers and which the platform gateway strips from external traffic. The value is not configurable, so point `dms_endpoint` and `kms_endpoint` at internal service addresses, not at a public gateway path that would reject or forward it. SymKMS calls from the service carry no credential."},"5090":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Route"},"5091":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Why"},"5092":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/:keyID/raw`"},"5093":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Returns raw key material."},"5094":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key`"},"5095":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Returns a device's raw key material. The Updates service uses it during a per-device build."},"5096":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`, `DELETE /symkms/v1/:keyID`, key assignment routes"},"5097":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Create, delete and assign encryption keys."},"5098":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`, `/decrypt`, `/mac`"},"5099":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Use stored keys on arbitrary data."},"5100":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`PUT /updates/v1/jobs/:jobID/transition`"},"5101":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Forges a job state change with no ownership check. Registered only when `enable_test_endpoints` is `true`: keep it `false`."},"5102":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Every `POST`, `PUT` and `DELETE` of `/updates/v1`"},"5103":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Build, launch, cancel and delete. Restrict them to operators."},"5104":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"`GET` of artifacts, descriptors and `artifacts-archive`"},"5105":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Expose firmware sources and sw-descriptions."},"5106":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Download routes with `:deviceID`"},"5107":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#routes-to-restrict","content":"Per-device builds are encrypted with that device's key, but the route itself checks nothing about who asks."},"5108":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"These are defence in depth, not a substitute for the gateway:"},"5109":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"A launch is addressed under its group: an operation on a launch through another group's path answers `404`, exactly as for a missing launch, and changes nothing."},"5110":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"Approval and error thresholds must be between 0 and 100."},"5111":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"In `native` mode, pack, group and device identifiers used in paths are validated so they cannot escape the storage directories, and a per-device pack never falls back to the shared build for a device."},"5112":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"An upload under a `.swu` name must really be a SWU: other content is refused with `400`."},"5113":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"An uploaded file larger than `max_artifact_size_mb` is refused with `413`."},"5114":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"In `hawkbit` mode the DDI artifact route serves a file only if the module is assigned to or installed on that device."},"5115":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#what-the-service-checks","content":"Anything that changes a built version is refused (`409`): versions are immutable."},"5116":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"With `presign.enabled`, a download is answered `302` to a short-lived URL of the S3 store. The service authorizes the caller first (the gateway for the static route and, in `hawkbit` mode, the device's assignment); the store then checks only the signature, so **the URL is a bearer capability**: whoever holds it can fetch that one object until it expires. The design keeps that acceptable:"},"5117":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The TTL is short (default 60 s). It bounds when a GET can **start**: a transfer in progress finishes after expiry, and a device that retries or resumes goes back to the static endpoint for a fresh URL. A URL already signed for the same object is reused while it has `min_remaining` validity left (default `min(25s, ttl/2)`); it grants no more than a fresh one."},"5118":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The signing credential must be **read-only** and different from the storage credential. At start-up the service probes with a write and refuses to run if the credential can write, is the storage's own, or is rejected by the store. A signature covers the method and the key, so a URL cannot be turned into a `PUT` or aimed at another object."},"5119":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The signed host is the store's **public** origin (`presign.public_endpoint`), because the signature covers the `Host` header."},"5120":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"It cannot be combined with at-rest encryption of the same store (devices would receive ciphertext)."},"5121":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"Redirect responses carry `Cache-Control: no-store`. `HEAD` requests are answered by the service, not redirected. If signing fails, the service streams the file instead of failing the update."},"5122":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"Rotate the signing credential by updating the files named by `access_key_id_file` and `secret_access_key_file`: they are re-read every minute."},"5123":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#presigned-download-urls","content":"The store itself must be reachable by devices at the public endpoint, and should accept only the read-only credential on the prefix it serves. Do not publish the store's console or S3 API with default credentials."},"5124":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Connection"},"5125":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Transport security"},"5126":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Postgres"},"5127":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"`sslmode=disable`, not configurable. Keep the database on a private network."},"5128":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Lamassu Device Manager"},"5129":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The Lamassu platform SDK client with its default settings."},"5130":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"Lamassu KMS"},"5131":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"`native` mode: certificate verification is **skipped** for the service's own calls, and the SWU signer script uses `curl -k`. `hawkbit` mode: the service's calls verify the certificate, the script still does not. Use an internal address you trust."},"5132":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"SymKMS"},"5133":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The scheme of `symkms_endpoint` (normally the service itself, over plain HTTP in the examples), with no credential. Raw key material crosses this connection: keep it on `localhost` or a private network."},"5134":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"hawkBit Management API"},"5135":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"HTTP Basic with `hawkbit.username` and `hawkbit.password`. Use HTTPS."},"5136":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"WFX"},"5137":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#outbound-connections","content":"The scheme of `wfx_endpoint` (plain HTTP in the examples), to the management listener."},"5138":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"`encryption.local_key`, S3 credentials and database passwords must come from a secret store, not from a file in the repository. The example configurations contain development values only. Prefer the `*_file` form of S3 and presign credentials, which the service re-reads every minute."},"5139":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"The Helm chart renders all of `config` into a ConfigMap. See Operations. Override its placeholder database password."},"5140":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"With `app.logs.level: debug` the service logs the whole configuration, secrets included, and in `native` mode it prints the `storage` block (with its password) to standard output at every start. Use `info` or higher in any environment whose logs are stored."},"5141":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"A lost `encryption.local_key` makes everything stored with it unreadable. See Backup and restore."},"5142":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"Signing keys stay in the Lamassu KMS: the service never holds the private key. Device encryption keys do live in SymKMS (optionally encrypted at rest), because packages must be encrypted with them."},"5143":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#secrets","content":"The container image does not drop privileges. Set a `securityContext` that suits your cluster."},"5144":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"The Management API user is a full administrator of hawkBit. Change the default (`admin`) credential, keep the API off the device network and serve it over HTTPS."},"5145":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"Devices authenticate to hawkBit, not to this service. hawkBit 1.1.0 has no anonymous mode: enable a target security token, a gateway token or the reverse-proxy header authenticator, and for the last restrict which addresses may set its headers. Leaving device authentication off, which is acceptable only on a throw-away test stack, lets anything that can reach hawkBit impersonate a device. See hawkBit mode."},"5146":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#hawkbit-mode","content":"hawkBit does not encrypt artifacts at rest. Enable default encryption in the bucket, or use encrypted (shared-key) packages."},"5147":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/security#request-limits","content":"A request body can be up to `max_artifact_size_mb` plus 1 MiB (10 GiB by default), and a request can take up to 6 hours, so large uploads work. Streamed uploads use temporary disk under `TMPDIR`. Apply tighter limits at the gateway for callers that are not trusted: there is no rate limiting in the service."},"5148":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"page","content":"Signing and encryption","breadcrumbs":["Docs","Platform","Updates","Concepts"],"tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption"},"5149":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-0","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Sign deliverables with the Lamassu KMS, encrypt them with a shared or per-device key, and manage device keys in SymKMS."},"5150":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-1","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing"},"5151":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-2","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#set-up-signing","content":"Set up signing"},"5152":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-3","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-the-key-and-a-certificate","content":"Create the key and a certificate"},"5153":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-4","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#configure-the-service","content":"Configure the service"},"5154":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-5","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"Send the signature fields in the build"},"5155":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-6","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Signed manifests"},"5156":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-7","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Encryption modes"},"5157":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-8","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Algorithms"},"5158":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-9","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#set-up-per-device-encryption","content":"Set up per-device encryption"},"5159":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-10","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-a-key-per-device","content":"Create a key per device"},"5160":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-11","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#assign-it-to-the-device","content":"Assign it to the device"},"5161":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-12","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#put-the-same-key-on-the-device","content":"Put the same key on the device"},"5162":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-13","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"Build"},"5163":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-14","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"SymKMS"},"5164":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-15","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","type":"heading","tags":[],"url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Request bodies"},"5165":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-16","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"This page explains how Lamassu Updates protects what it delivers: which keys sign and encrypt a package, how to configure them, and what each backend supports. There are three independent layers."},"5166":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-17","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Layer"},"5167":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-18","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Protects"},"5168":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-19","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Configured in"},"5169":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-20","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Package signing"},"5170":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-21","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"That the package came from you and is unmodified"},"5171":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-22","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"A signing key and certificate in the Lamassu KMS, plus `kms_endpoint` and `sign_script_path`"},"5172":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-23","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Package encryption"},"5173":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-24","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The contents of the package in transit and on the device's download path"},"5174":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-25","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The build request, plus a key in SymKMS"},"5175":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-26","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"At-rest encryption"},"5176":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-27","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"Artifacts, builds and keys stored by the service"},"5177":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-28","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","content":"The `encryption` block of each blob storage block"},"5178":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-29","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing is optional. When you ask for it, `swugenerator` calls the configured signer script (`sign_script_path`, which is `sign_kms.sh`), and the script asks the Lamassu KMS (`kms_endpoint`) to sign. The private key never reaches the machine that builds the package."},"5179":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-30","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"For `.swu` builds both settings must be set: the service refuses a signing request when either is missing."},"5180":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-31","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Signing a manifest, a `non-swu` package or a hawkBit `raw` module calls the KMS directly from the service and needs only `kms_endpoint`."},"5181":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-32","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signing","content":"Select the key in the build request with `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` (default `RSASSA_PSS_SHA_256`; `-` and `_` are interchangeable) and `signature_certificate` (PEM). The three fields go together: a request with a key but no algorithm or certificate is refused, never built unsigned."},"5182":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-33","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-the-key-and-a-certificate","content":"In the Lamassu KMS, create (or choose) the signing key and issue a certificate for it from a CA your devices trust. See Keys and cryptographic engines. The key ID is your `signature_key_id`."},"5183":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-34","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#configure-the-service","content":"Set `kms_endpoint` and `sign_script_path` (`/app/sign_kms.sh` in the image). `swugenerator` calls the script with the key ID, the KMS URL, the algorithm and the path of the certificate file, which the script requires. The script writes a debug log to `/tmp/sign_kms_debug.log`."},"5184":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-35","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"Include `signature_key_id`, `signature_alg_name` and `signature_certificate` in the build body. In `hawkbit` mode they go in the module build body."},"5185":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-36","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"SWUpdate verifies a `.swu` with a CMS `SignedData` signature, and the service requires CMS for the manifests it signs itself. A Lamassu KMS that ignores the `Accept` header and answers with a bare signature in a JSON envelope produces a signature no device can verify. Where the service signs itself (version manifests, set manifests, raw-module checksums) it refuses such an answer and the operation fails with `the KMS did not return a PKCS7/CMS signature`. The SWU signer script does not check the format: it unwraps the answer and embeds it, so against a KMS without CMS support a `.swu` build can succeed and still be rejected by a device that sets `public-key-file`. Test one signed build on a real device before you rely on a KMS version."},"5186":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-37","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"`sign_kms_nocms.sh` is a variant of the script that takes no certificate. The service's own manifest signing is separate: it always sends the certificate and refuses to sign without one."},"5187":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-38","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#send-the-signature-fields-in-the-build","content":"TLS towards the KMS: in `native` mode the service's KMS client skips certificate verification, and `sign_kms.sh` calls `curl -k`. In `hawkbit` mode the service's own KMS calls verify the certificate, but the SWU signer script still uses `curl -k`. Reach the KMS over an internal address you trust. See Security."},"5188":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-39","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Each built version also has a **manifest**, an anti-rollback record of what the version contains: name, group, version, packaging, artifacts with their SHA-256, the deliverable and, in `hawkbit` mode, the exact modules and versions that compose the set. A manifest is valid for 5 years (`expires_at`). It is signed with the KMS key when the build carried signing fields, and stored unsigned otherwise (the service logs a warning). If a signing key is configured but the manifest cannot be signed, the build fails."},"5189":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-40","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"Read it with:"},"5190":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-41","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#signed-manifests","content":"The response has `manifest` (the exact bytes the signature covers), `signature` (base64 CMS), `algorithm`, `certificate` (PEM), `signed_at` and `expires_at`. In `hawkbit` mode `stale: true` means a signed manifest exists but the set's contents changed since, so the manifest returned describes the set as it is now. The `artifact_signatures` capability reports whether the active backend provides it."},"5191":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-42","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Mode"},"5192":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-43","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"What you get"},"5193":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-44","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"`native`"},"5194":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-45","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"`hawkbit`"},"5195":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-46","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"None"},"5196":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-47","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One unencrypted deliverable"},"5197":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-48","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5198":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-49","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5199":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-50","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Shared"},"5200":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-51","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One deliverable encrypted with one key, served to every device"},"5201":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-52","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5202":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-53","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes, through the module build endpoints, when the build pipeline is configured"},"5203":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-54","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Per-device"},"5204":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-55","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"One deliverable per device, each encrypted with that device's own key from SymKMS"},"5205":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-56","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Yes"},"5206":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-57","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"No"},"5207":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-58","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"The build body decides the mode:"},"5208":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-59","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**Shared**: send `user`, `encryption_key_name` and `encryption_alg_name`. A `.swu` build is refused without the algorithm. A `.../package` build picks AES-GCM from the key length and only records the name you send."},"5209":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-60","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**Per-device**: send `encryption_alg_name` **without** `user` or `encryption_key_name`. This holds for `.../package` too: sending the algorithm is what selects per-device mode, and omitting it builds an unencrypted package."},"5210":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-61","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"**None**: send neither."},"5211":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-62","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"Other build fields: `sw_desc_encrypted` also encrypts the sw-description itself, and `selected_artifact_ids` lists the artifacts the build includes. In `native` mode a `.swu` build with no selected artifacts fails."},"5212":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-63","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"In `hawkbit` mode `POST .../swu` returns `501`. Send the same signing and encryption fields to the module build instead: `POST /updates/v1/softwaremodules/by-id/:moduleID/build` (for `swu-build` and `raw` modules). See hawkBit mode."},"5213":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-64","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#encryption-modes","content":"The sw-description must mark the artifacts to encrypt with `encrypted = true;`. A per-device build is refused when no artifact is marked, because the key alone does nothing."},"5214":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-65","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"The `algorithm` of a SymKMS key and the `encryption_alg_name` of a build use these names."},"5215":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-66","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Algorithm"},"5216":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-67","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"Key length"},"5217":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-68","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-128-CBC`, `AES-128-CTR`, `AES-128-GCM`"},"5218":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-69","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"16 bytes"},"5219":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-70","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-192-CBC`, `AES-192-CTR`, `AES-192-GCM`"},"5220":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-71","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"24 bytes"},"5221":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-72","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`AES-256-CBC`, `AES-256-CTR`, `AES-256-GCM`"},"5222":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-73","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"32 bytes"},"5223":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-74","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`ASCON-128`, `ASCON-128A`"},"5224":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-75","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"16 bytes"},"5225":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-76","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"`ASCON-80PQ`"},"5226":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-77","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"20 bytes"},"5227":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-78","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**SymKMS key names**: matching ignores case, and `_` and `-` are interchangeable (`aes_256_gcm` is stored as `AES-256-GCM`). The separators of the name must still be there: `ascon128a` is not `ASCON-128A`. A key whose length does not match its algorithm is rejected when it is created."},"5228":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-79","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**Build names**: `encryption_alg_name` is passed to `swugenerator` as it is. Case is ignored, but the hyphens are required: `aes-256-gcm` works, `AES_256_GCM` is rejected. If the name differs from the algorithm stored with the key, the service logs a warning and uses the name from the request."},"5229":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-80","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"**`non-swu` packages** (`.../package`, and `hawkbit` `raw` modules) are always encrypted with **AES-GCM**, chosen by key length (16, 24 or 32 bytes). The requested name is only recorded, and a 20-byte Ascon-80pq key is refused. The result is `nonce || ciphertext`."},"5230":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-81","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#algorithms","content":"The service generates the IV or nonce. In `native` mode the algorithm and, for shared-key packs, the IV are passed to the device in the WFX job. A per-device build draws a fresh IV for each device and does not record it in the job, so the job carries the algorithm only. The job fields are listed in Connect a device."},"5231":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-82","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#create-a-key-per-device","content":"In SymKMS, `POST /symkms/v1/` with `user_id`, an `algorithm` from the table and a `key` (hex or base64) of the right length."},"5232":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-83","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#assign-it-to-the-device","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/keys/:keyID` with a body `{\"purpose\":\"firmware-encryption\"}` and an optional `expires_at` (RFC 3339). A per-device build asks for each device's `firmware-encryption` key."},"5233":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-84","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#put-the-same-key-on-the-device","content":"In the form SWUpdate expects (its `-K` key file, with the key, IV and algorithm)."},"5234":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-85","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"Send `encryption_alg_name` and no `user` or `encryption_key_name`. The sw-description must mark an artifact `encrypted = true;`."},"5235":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-86","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Key purposes.** The conventional purposes are `firmware-encryption`, `config-encryption` and `mac-verification`. The purpose is a placeholder: any value is accepted, and a binding with an empty purpose acts as a wildcard that matches any lookup. This is intentional while per-purpose keys are rolled out. An exact (case-insensitive) match wins over a wildcard, and among equals the most recent assignment wins. Expired or revoked bindings are skipped."},"5236":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-87","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Coverage.** A device with no `firmware-encryption` key is skipped (the reason reads `no firmware-encryption key assigned` for `.swu` builds). The build still succeeds if at least one device was covered, and the pack records the coverage: read `built_device_count`, `total_device_count` and `uncovered_devices` on it. A launch on a pack with uncovered devices is refused with `400`, and there is no override: assign the missing keys and build again. If no device was covered, the build itself fails."},"5237":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-88","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#build","content":"**Cost.** A per-device build runs one `swugenerator` process per device, in parallel up to the CPU available to the container. On a 100 MB artifact, one device costs roughly half a second of encryption, plus about three seconds more if the sw-description asks for gzip compression. Size the container accordingly: see Resource sizing. Builds of the same pack are serialized: a second build or version bump while one runs answers `409`."},"5238":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-89","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"SymKMS is the embedded symmetric key service, served by the same process under `/symkms/v1`. It stores keys, assigns them to devices, and can also encrypt, decrypt and compute MACs. Keys are stored in the `symkms` blob store, optionally with at-rest encryption. Create keys with the correct length for their algorithm: random bytes, never a passphrase."},"5239":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-90","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Task"},"5240":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-91","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Route"},"5241":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-92","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Store a key"},"5242":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-93","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`"},"5243":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-94","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"List keys of a user"},"5244":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-95","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/?user_id=...`"},"5245":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-96","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Delete a key"},"5246":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-97","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`DELETE /symkms/v1/:keyID?user_id=...`"},"5247":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-98","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Assign or revoke a key for a device"},"5248":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-99","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST` or `DELETE /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/keys/:keyID`"},"5249":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-100","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"A device's active key (privileged, returns key material)"},"5250":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-101","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key?purpose=...`"},"5251":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-102","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Which devices use a key"},"5252":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-103","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/by-key/:keyID`"},"5253":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-104","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"A device's key bindings"},"5254":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-105","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID`"},"5255":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-106","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"Encrypt, decrypt"},"5256":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-107","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`, `POST /symkms/v1/decrypt`"},"5257":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-108","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"MAC and verify"},"5258":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-109","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#symkms","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac`, `POST /symkms/v1/mac/verify` (and the `/file` variants)"},"5259":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-110","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Route"},"5260":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-111","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"Body (JSON)"},"5261":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-112","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/`"},"5262":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-113","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `algorithm`, `key` (hex or base64; hex is tried first), optional `id`. `user_id`, `algorithm` and `key` are required."},"5263":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-114","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/encrypt`"},"5264":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-115","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `algorithm`, `plaintext` (base64), optional `iv`, optional `format`."},"5265":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-116","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/decrypt`"},"5266":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-117","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `algorithm`, `ciphertext`, `iv`, optional `format`."},"5267":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-118","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac`"},"5268":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-119","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`user_id`, `key_name`, `mac_algorithm`, `data` (base64). The MAC is returned as hex."},"5269":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-120","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`POST /symkms/v1/mac/verify`"},"5270":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-121","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"The same as `/mac`, plus `mac` (hex)."},"5271":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-122","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`format` is `ciphertext` (hex, the default), `base64`, or `cms` (`pkcs7` is an alias): a PEM-encoded CMS structure that embeds the algorithm and IV. With `cms`, `decrypt` can omit `algorithm` and `iv`."},"5272":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-123","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"The server generates the nonce for GCM, CTR and Ascon: **a caller-supplied `iv` is refused** for those algorithms. Only CBC accepts one (16 bytes). The response carries the `iv` used (hex)."},"5273":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-124","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`mac_algorithm` is `HMAC-SHA3-256`, `AES-CMAC` or `ASCON-MAC`. The `/file` variants take the data as `multipart/form-data`."},"5274":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-125","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption#request-bodies","content":"`GET /symkms/v1/:keyID/raw?user_id=...` and `GET /symkms/v1/inventory/:deviceID/key` return raw key material and are privileged: the Updates service itself calls them during a build. The service has no authentication of its own, so restrict these routes at a gateway. See Security."},"5275":{"id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption-126","page_id":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-encryption","tags":[],"type":"text","url":"/docs/pr-preview/pr-56/platform/updates/signing-and-enc