n attribute belonging to another."],[479,"HTTP rules"],[571,"HTTP rules do not point directly at tables. They reference a route schema and grant its logical actions. Job Manager's policies are an example: they distinguish reading, creating, updating and deleting workflows or jobs."],[519,"HTTP rules primarily answer &#x2A;*\"can this identity call this API operation?\"**. On their own they do not produce filters over the external service's database. To limit a route to a specific device, tenant or client, either the schema declares a constraint relating a request value to a normalized attribute of the principal, or the policy pins the request value to a literal with `param_constraints`. The first scopes each identity to its own resources through a single grant; the second restricts a grant to a fixed value regardless of who holds it."],[5278,"HTTP status codes"],[1356,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's CA service."],[1352,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's Device Manager."],[1348,"HTTP URL of Lamassu's DMS Manager service."],[398,"I cannot sign in"],[3977,"I want to..."],[1280,"IAM action"],[1362,"IAM actions"],[1638,"ID created automatically and correct DMS."],[892,"ID of the signing CA."],[1088,"ID, owning DMS, certificate CN and bound serial."],[2002,"Identify a certificate by issuer and serial; a name can correspond to several renewals. Check which certificate the consumer actually uses and which occupies the device’s active identity. Identity history and the certificate inventory answer different questions."],[2052,"Identify DMSs, devices and services that trust that chain."],[2436,"Identify the certificate"],[1878,"Identify the certificates, devices and consumers that depend on the CA. Prepare a replacement authority and chain when necessary."],[861,"Identify the fleet"],[702,"Identify the operation"],[359,"Identity"],[1960,"Identity"],[5032,"Identity and namespace for Kubernetes leader election. The Helm chart sets them. If unset, the hostname and the service-account namespace file 