not in the file (see the `*_file` credentials above)."],[3334,"With `auto` off, hawkBit pauses after each group. Each `rollout` call releases the next one:"],[2875,"With `auto` on, one `rollout` call starts the launch and the following batches are released by flow 4. A launch with `scheduled_at` is started by the scheduled-launch trigger on the leader replica once that time passes."],[3420,"With `auto` on, the service sends the next batch itself once enough of the current one succeeded. `approval_threshold` is the percentage of the batch that must succeed (0 or 100 mean all of it). `error_threshold` applies to every launch, `auto` or not: the launch is cancelled once the number of failed devices reaches that percentage of **all** devices, rounded up. With 4 devices at 75%, the third failure cancels it."],[844,"With `CLIENT_CERTIFICATE`, the device presents its initial certificate and proves key possession through TLS. The DMS validates it against admission CAs. In the inspected flow, the validator receives one leaf credential: configure and test the direct issuer for the simple case; sending more intermediates does not establish delivery to the service."],[3707,"With `dms_endpoint` set, every read of a group's devices creates the missing targets (controller ID = device ID) and tags them `group:<id>`. A device that cannot be reconciled is excluded from that read and logged. Without `dms_endpoint`, groups are the existing `group:<id>` tags."],[5116,"With `presign.enabled`, a download is answered `302` to a short-lived URL of the S3 store. The service authorizes the caller first (the gateway for the static route and, in `hawkbit` mode, the device's assignment); the store then checks only the signature, so **the URL is a bearer capability**: whoever holds it can fetch that one object until it expires. The design keeps that acceptable:"],[2147,"With `regenerate_on_revoke`, the event handler requests a new CRL upon revocation or reactivation from `CertificateHold` to `ACTIVE`. This happens after the status change and has its own failure paths: if it fails (missing role, invalid signer), the event is retried and, once retries are exhausted, moves to the failed-events queue. Confirming revocation does not establish that the new CRL is already published or that all clients have downloaded it."],[5676,"With `tls.certManagerOptions.issuer` empty, the chart creates a release-scoped self-signed issuer, for example `lamassu-downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer`. The legacy literal `downstream-ca-selfsigned-issuer` is still accepted and resolves to it."],[192,"With both `--tls-crt` and `--tls-key`, Fastlane creates the `downstream-provided-crt` Secret and configures `tls.type: external`."],[1138,"With certificate authentication, review `enable_expired_renewal` and whether Gateway permits presenting that credential. Revocation, subject and the remaining checks still apply."],[946,"With credentials configured, they are sent regardless of the URL scheme: an `http://` webhook receives the API key or bearer token in cleartext, and mTLS has no effect because no TLS handshake takes place, so the client certificate is never presented. Prefer `https://` for `url`, `oidc_well_known` and the token endpoint it advertises."],[5689,"With Helm, enable the hook for the upgrade in step 2; without Helm, run the tool by hand."],[996,"With initial `CLIENT_CERTIFICATE` authentication, send the Base64-encoded DER CSR using `Content-Type: application/pkcs10`:"],[3887,"With Leases, one Lease per role is created in the pod's namespace (`lamassu-updates-wfx-event-consumer` and `lamassu-updates-scheduled-launch-trigger`), and `kubectl get lease` shows the pod that leads (`POD_NAME` is the holder). The lease lasts 15 s and is renewed within 10 s, so a failover takes about that long. With the database lock, a standby retries every 15 s and the leader verifies every 5 s that its connection is still alive."],[3764,"With local storage on one `ReadWriteOnce` volume, only one `native` replica can run. Move `artifacts`, `builds` and `symkms` to S3 to scale out. See Operations."],[231,"With no CA Secret configured, the event-bus clients use the system-trusted CAs. To trust a private CA, create a Secret in the release namespace containing the CA certificate in PEM format and set `amqp.ca.secretName` (and `amqp.ca.certificateKey` if the data key is not `ca.crt`)."],[4968,"With no credential set, the AWS default chain applies (environment, IRSA, instance profile)."],[5736,"With release `lamassu` and the default chart name, the new PVCs are `golang-engine-storage-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-lamassu-va-0`; with release `prod` they are `golang-engine-storage-prod-lamassu-kms-0` and `local-crl-file-storage-prod-lamassu-va-0`. Confirm both old and new PVCs exist before continuing. If `claims_ok` prints `ABORT`, the block stops before listing the claims: either a StatefulSet lookup failed, or a new claim resolves to the 3.8.0 claim. In the second case the copy would verify against itself and the final cleanup would delete the live volume. The chart always appends `-kms` and `-va` to the release-scoped name, so a collision means the claims are not what this guide expects; investigate before going on. Item 3 runs the same check and refuses to create the helper pod, so nothing touches the volumes. The check returns instead of calling `exit`, which would close your shell and lose the variables set so far. If you only migrate one of the two services, drop the other one's claims from the commands that follow."],[4090,"With S3 storage and presigning enabled, a `GET` can answer `302` to a signed URL of the object store, with `Cache-Control: no-store`. The caller is authorized first; the store then only checks the signature. A `HEAD` is never redirected. Native mode signs build outputs (`.swu` and packages); hawkBit mode signs the objects of hawkBit's S3 artifact plugin. If signing fails, the service streams the file instead."],[4985,"With S3 storage, a download can be answered with `302` to a short-lived signed URL of the store instead of streaming the bytes through the service. The caller is authorized first, as for any download. Native mode signs build outputs (`builds.presign`); `hawkbit` mode signs the objects of hawkBit's S3 plugin (`hawkbit.artifact_store.presign`). Artifact downloads by ID in `native` mode are always streamed."],[2874,"With the `phased` workflow a job starts in `CREATED`, and some transitions need a person or system to confirm them in WFX. This service does not advance them. The `download-install` workflow, used by `non-swu` packs, runs `DOWNLOAD → DOWNLOADING → DOWNLOADED → INSTALL → INSTALLING → INSTALLED`."],[3714,"With the plugin and `hawkbit.artifact_store.presign` configured, downloads of module artifacts are answered `302` to a short-lived signed URL of the bucket instead of streaming through hawkBit or this service. Devices keep the artifact link hawkBit gave them: the adapter serves that one DDI route (`<ddi path>/:tenant/controller/v1/:controllerId/softwaremodules/:id/artifacts/:filename`), checks that the module is assigned to or installed on that device (otherwise `404`) and redirects. For this to work, the gateway must route that path to Lamassu Updates and the rest of the DDI to hawkBit. See Configuration and Security."],[1633,"With the same server still running, test that a request without a client certificate is rejected:"],[3547,"Without `auto`, each call dispatches the next batch (the canary first, if you set one). With `auto: true`, call it once to start the first batch: the service then releases the later batches itself as the approval threshold is met, and further calls answer `400`. If the launch has a future `scheduled_at`, the call is accepted but does nothing: the service starts it by itself at that time (native checks every 30 seconds; hawkBit's own scheduler starts the rollout)."],[3430,"Without `workflow`, a `swu` pack uses `phased`. Only the pack's current version can be forced, unless the pack was created with `allow_previous_version_download`."],[2869,"Without signing fields the manifest is stored unsigned. If a signing key is given but no certificate, the build fails instead."],[5747,"Without the chart's database job, no tool moves data between databases: the migration tooling only applies migrations to a schema that already exists. Move each per-service database into its `pki` schema yourself, preserving structure, indexes, constraints, data and migration history, with writes stopped and a verified backup in hand."],[193,"Without them, it configures cert-manager with a self-signed issuer. This is suitable for a lab but will not be trusted by clients until you distribute the CA. Use Helm when you need a corporate Issuer, public ACME issuer or an existing Secret managed by another system."],[337,"Workflow"],[3035,"Workflow"],[2752,"Workflow file"],[2708,"Workflow terminal state"],[4146,"Workflows registered in WFX, as `{\"content\": [...]}`. Empty in hawkBit mode"],[3903,"Written to standard output: the application log (level `app.logs.level`) and an access log of every request. At `debug` the start-up log includes the whole configuration, secrets too."],[5331,"Wrong bucket, endpoint or credentials, or the bucket does not exist"],[433,"wrong credentials or DNS for PostgreSQL or RabbitMQ;"],[5424,"Wrong key ID or `user`, or the endpoint points at another instance"],[473,"X.509 principals"],[1311,"Yes"],[1315,"Yes"],[1319,"Yes"],[1343,"Yes"],[1347,"Yes"],[1351,"Yes"],[1355,"Yes"],[2574,"Yes"],[2578,"Yes"],[2582,"Yes"],[2586,"Yes"],[2590,"Yes"],[2594,"Yes"],[2598,"Yes"],[2602,"Yes"],[4472,"Yes"],[4475,"Yes"],[4478,"Yes"],[4481,"Yes"],[4655,"Yes"],[4656,"Yes"],[4658,"Yes"],[4659,"Yes"],[4661,"Yes"],[4662,"Yes"],[4664,"Yes"],[4667,"Yes"],[4670,"Yes"],[4671,"Yes"],[4673,"Yes"],[4676,"Yes"],[4679,"Yes"],[4682,"Yes"],[4688,"Yes"],[4691,"Yes"],[4692,"Yes"],[4694,"Yes"],[4695,"Yes"],[4697,"Yes"],[4698,"Yes"],[4700,"Yes"],